# No bindings live here anymore.
#
# skhd is a CGEventTap, and macOS Secure Event Input blinds every event tap
# session-wide: while some app holds SE (kitty's toggle, a password prompt,
# loginwindow's lock screen), macOS delivers no key events to taps at all. On
# 2026-09-26 that took every binding in this file down at once, and it stayed
# down until a reboot, because a leaked SE token cannot be released by anything
# but a new session.
#
# So every hotkey now lives where SE cannot reach it:
#
#   Option+1..0         native macOS "Switch to Desktop 1..10" hotkeys
#                       (symbolichotkeys ids 118..127, enabled in
#                        ~/Library/Preferences/com.apple.symbolichotkeys.plist
#                        and registered live via SkyLight's
#                        CGSSetSymbolicHotKeyEnabled). loginwindow-level, so SE
#                        cannot eat them.
#   Option+Shift+1..0   Karabiner-Elements -> scripts/yabai_move_window_to_space.sh N
#   Option+H/J/K/L      focus window west/south/north/east
#   Option+Shift+H/J/K/L  swap window west/south/north/east
#                       yabai's west|south|north|east are TREE selectors, and
#                       float layout has no tree, so these fall back to a
#                       geometry pick among the visible windows on the Space
#                       (centre-based; overlapping windows can surprise).
#   Option+Shift+M      maximize the focused window into its Space (grid
#                       1:1:0:0:1:1). If that Space is bsp/stack it is switched to
#                       float first -- tiling re-flows and would undo the grid,
#                       leaving the window looking floated but not maximized.
#   Option+Shift+T      toggle the current Space between float and bsp (yabai
#                       layout; scripts/yabai_toggle_layout.sh). Note that bsp
#                       hands window placement to yabai, which the yabairc below
#                       deliberately avoids, and switching back to float does not
#                       restore the frames your windows had before.
#   Option+Shift+R      restart yabai (scripts/yabai_restart.sh) -- the remedy for
#                       its stale window records, where an app that recreated its
#                       window reads in yabai as 0x0 and every geometry command
#                       (fill, move, resize, bsp placement) silently does nothing.
#
# Everything except the desktop switcher goes through Karabiner-Elements: the
# window actions via scripts/yabai_window_action.sh, the layout toggle via
# scripts/yabai_toggle_layout.sh, the yabai restart via scripts/yabai_restart.sh.
# Karabiner grabs the keyboard at the HID layer (kIOHIDOptionsTypeSeizeDevice) and
# re-injects through its DriverKit virtual HID device with no CGEventTap
# fallback, which is why it keeps remapping while SE is on. The rules are in
# ~/.config/karabiner/karabiner.json, duplicated in both profiles so switching
# profiles does not lose them.
#
# skhd is installed but disabled: `launchctl disable gui/$(id -u)/com.koekeishiya.skhd`
# plus a bootout of the same label. Its launchd plist is still in
# ~/Library/LaunchAgents, so it comes back with:
#   launchctl enable gui/$(id -u)/com.koekeishiya.skhd
#   launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.koekeishiya.skhd.plist
# Add bindings here only if you want that fallback; they work whenever SE happens
# to be off. scripts/ensure_skhd_running.sh still runs (it detects and reports a
# stuck SE token and pins kitty's SE preference to false) -- it just no longer
# starts or supervises skhd.
#
# Layout note: yabai runs in float layout (see ~/.config/yabai/yabairc) -- there
# is no tiling, so no ghost-window squeezing and no yabai-fix-layout.sh watchdog.
# macOS Tiling handles window placement.
